}^mK_k(i_{k-1},i_k)$; summing over all paths gives $1$ by the normalization of $\\mu_0$ and the row sums of the kernels.\n\nWork on the system is positive when energy is supplied to it, and heat into the system is positive when a bath transition raises its energy. Define $W(\\omega)=\\sum_{k=1}^m[E_k(i_{k-1})-E_{k-1}(i_{k-1})]$ and $Q_{\\mathrm{in}}(\\omega)=\\sum_{k=1}^m[E_k(i_k)-E_k(i_{k-1})]$, both in joules. Define $F_k=-\\beta^{-1}\\log Z_k$ and $\\Delta F=F_m-F_0=-\\beta^{-1}\\log(Z_m/Z_0)$. These are finite-model quantities; their physical interpretation is conditional on the adopted preparation and transition assumptions.",
