          "reason": "For every path $\\omega=(i_0,\\ldots,i_m)$ of [[def-td-driven-finite-path-model]], the endpoint energy change is $E_m(i_m)-E_0(i_0)=W(\\omega)+Q_{\\mathrm{in}}(\\omega)$, with the stated sign convention. Boundary nonempty-choice: No choice principle is used; the finite data are fixed and all sums are finite. Item: pthm-td-finite-pathwise-first-law.",
          "case_scope": {
