            "source_excerpt": "Assume the setup of [[def-td-driven-finite-path-model]], the canonical initial law of [[post-td-canonical-protocol-preparation]], the stationarity model of [[post-td-stationary-bath-kernel]], and, additionally, $\\pi_k(i)K_k(i,j)=\\pi_k(j)K_k(j,i)$ for every $k,i,j$. For every forward path with positive probability, define its reverse probability by $P_R(\\omega^R)=\\pi_m(i_m)\\prod_{k=1}^mK_k(i_k,i_{k-1})$. Then $P_R(\\omega^R)>0$ and $P_F(\\omega)/P_R(\\omega^R)=e^{\\beta(W(\\omega)-\\Delta F)}$. Consequently, at each work value $w$, $P_F(W=w)=e^{\\beta(w-\\Delta F)}P_R(W_R=-w)$. The reverse protocol first applies the stage-$k$ reverse transition at fixed $E_k$, then reverses the quench $E_k\\to E_{k-1}$; its work is $W_R(\\omega^R)=-W(\\omega)$.",
