      "finite_checks": [],
      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-19",
        "notes": "Checked reverse product defines a normalized law by row-stochastic kernels in reverse stage order. Positive canonical weights and detailed balance pair supports in both directions, including zero transitions; hence zero forward paths also have zero reversed mass. Endpoint Gibbs ratio and kernel ratios telescope with heat-in sign to beta(W-Delta F). Reverse transition precedes quench at i_(k-1), so reversed work is -W. Finite summation proves identity for all real w, including unattained values where both masses vanish. No convergence, AC or empirical input is used. Clarified kernel definition is used exactly as specified."
      }
