          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume the Axiom of Choice [[def-axiom-of-choice]]: every family of nonempty sets has a choice function. It is inherited from the Brownian and Itô-integral suppliers used for the stationary Gaussian model.\n\nUnder [[post-td-linear-ornstein-uhlenbeck-bath]], prepare $X_0\\sim N(0,V)$ independently of future Brownian increments, where $V=k_{\\mathrm B}T_b/k$. Then the conditional linear model has stationary covariance $C(\\tau)=Ve^{-\\mu k|\\tau|}$. With angular-frequency convention $S(\\omega)=(2\\pi)^{-1}\\int_{\\mathbb R}C(\\tau)e^{i\\omega\\tau}\\,d\\tau$, its spectrum is $S(\\omega)=\\mu k_{\\mathrm B}T_b/(\\pi[(\\mu k)^2+\\omega^2])$. For every averaging time $T>0$, $\\operatorname{Var}(T^{-1}\\int_0^T X_t\\,dt)\\le 2k_{\\mathrm B}T_b/(\\mu k^2T)$. These are model predictions, not reported observations.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "0bec25168f15be077a4a3412adab04c620d13147ef144e226c444dceed8797b3",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
